HALT(1)                        P32W Unix                         HALT(1)

NAME
       halt - stop the machine at once

SYNOPSIS
       halt

DESCRIPTION
       halt is for root. It calls sync(2), then the reboot(2)
       system call, which writes every mounted filesystem out,
       marks each one clean in its superblock, prints

              P32W Unix: halted

       on the console and stops the processor. The emulators exit;
       on the real machine the CPU halts until reset.

       No one is warned and no process is told: programs running
       on either terminal simply stop. Use shutdown(1) to warn the
       users and end their processes first.

EXIT STATUS
       Only on failure: 1, with halt: and the reason, if the caller
       is not root.

SEE ALSO
       reboot(1), shutdown(1), sync(1), reboot(2), init(8), fsck(8)

BUGS
       There are no options (no -n, -q). Files open for writing are
       not closed by their programs, so data still buffered inside
       a program (stdio) is lost.
